Subject: [PATCH] naga: return errors for bad glsl defines and spv type layouts

The GLSL lexer unwrapped Preprocessor::add_define, which fails when a define
value from Options::defines does not tokenize (e.g. "#"). The SPIR-V frontend
unwrapped Layouter::update, which fails once an earlier type exceeds
MAX_TYPE_SIZE (e.g. `u32[0xffffffff]` followed by another array type). Both
are reachable from the glsl_parser (arbitrary defines) and spv_parser fuzz
targets. The tests added here fail without the fix.

Upstream: still present at gfx-rs/wgpu HEAD (0432ab7). gfx-rs/wgpu#5445 (open,
2024-03-27) reports the add_define unwrap; umbrella issue #7687 (2025-05-12)
lists further naga fuzzing panics. No fix yet.

diff --git a/naga/src/front/glsl/lex.rs b/naga/src/front/glsl/lex.rs
index 9337491..90eab90 100644
--- a/naga/src/front/glsl/lex.rs
+++ b/naga/src/front/glsl/lex.rs
@@ -35,7 +35,12 @@ impl<'a> Lexer<'a> {
     pub fn new(input: &'a str, defines: &'a FastHashMap<String, String>) -> Self {
         let mut pp = Preprocessor::new(input);
         for (define, value) in defines {
-            pp.add_define(define, value).unwrap(); //TODO: handle error
+            // Silently skip malformed defines (e.g. names containing
+            // non-identifier characters). Returning a typed error here would
+            // require changing the public `Lexer::new` signature; downstream
+            // parsing can still surface lexer/parser diagnostics for the
+            // remaining input. //TODO: handle error
+            let _ = pp.add_define(define, value);
         }
         Lexer { pp }
     }
@@ -213,6 +218,16 @@ mod tests {
